{"t":"2026-09-26T06:25:51.985Z","kind":"model","text":"```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"note\",\n  \"text\": \"Reading the landscape: a river meadow with five existing structures—Parliament (modernist, 15 tall, snow), two riverside pavilions (wood), Sentinel (modest wood tower), and Meadow Pavilion (organic timber west). The area is 92% free ground. Gaps: no medium-height structure, nothing built with dirt/grass, no tall landmark (envelope allows 64). The Parliament dominates; others respond quietly. I should build something that answers the modernist geometry with organic form—perhaps a tall, asymmetrical earthwork or ruin-like structure in stone and moss, bridging the gap between the Parliament's scale and the pavilions' intimacy. Will scout the river and Parliament location first.\"\n}\n```"}
